    <h1 class="rv in" style="font-size:clamp(2.2rem,5vw,4rem);max-width:20ch">Can You Do a Boat Trip on Your Arrival or Departure Day in Madeira?</h1>
    <div class="artmeta rv in d1"><span>3 December 2026</span><span>5 min read</span><span>Funchal · Madeira</span></div>
  </div>
</header>

<section class="pad">
  <div class="wrap">
    <article class="article rv">
      <p class="lede">On your departure day, yes: the 10:00 Day Trip ends by 12:30 or 13:00, which leaves time for a flight in the late afternoon. On your arrival day it is a gamble, because wind delays and diversions at Madeira&#x27;s airport are common enough to make you miss a boat booked a few hours after landing.</p>

      <h2>How far is the airport from the marina?</h2><p>Madeira's airport is in Santa Cruz, roughly 16 to 18 km east of central Funchal. A taxi usually takes 20 to 30 minutes to the seafront, longer at busy times. There is an airport bus as well, slower but cheaper.</p><p>From most hotels in the centre you can walk to Marina do Funchal, which sits halfway along the seafront. The drive is not what needs planning. Everything around the flight is. Our guide on <a href="/posts/getting-to-madeira-guide">getting to Madeira</a> covers flights and transfers in more detail.</p><h2>Why is the arrival day the risky one?</h2><p>Because Madeira's airport has to stop landings when the wind is too strong. The runway runs along the coast below steep slopes, and the airport works with mandatory wind limits, set by the authorities rather than left to each pilot. When the wind is over the limit, planes circle, wait or divert to Porto Santo, the Canary Islands or mainland Portugal, and some flights are cancelled.</p><p>It is not rare. In March 2026 more than 160 flights were cancelled over the month, and smaller spells of delays and diversions happen through the year, in summer too. Nobody can tell you weeks ahead which day it will be.</p><p>That matters for one reason. You can cancel a Chifbay trip for free until 24 hours before it leaves. A flight that goes wrong on the morning itself is already past that point. That alone is why we suggest not booking a boat for the day you land.</p><p>Then add the smaller risks: a bag that does not arrive with the swimwear in it, a tired group after a very early start, a hotel room that is not ready until mid afternoon.</p><h2>What happens if your flight is diverted on the way in?</h2><p>You wait, usually somewhere else. A plane sent to Porto Santo often sits on the ground until the wind drops, then tries again. A plane sent to the Canaries or the mainland may not come back the same day. Either way, the afternoon you planned is gone.</p><p>If it happens and you have a trip booked, message us on WhatsApp as soon as you know, so the skipper is not waiting on an empty pontoon. Then look at the forecast for the rest of your stay and pick a new day with a calm sea.</p><h2>If you still want the arrival day, which trip fits?</h2><p>Only the Sunset Trip, and only if you land early. It leaves 1 h 15 before sunset, which is around 16:45 in December and around 20:00 in June. Count backwards from that and allow for:</p><ol><li>some delay on the flight itself;</li><li>bags and the taxi, an hour or so from landing to hotel;</li><li>check in and a change of clothes;</li><li>15 minutes on the pontoon before departure.</li></ol><p>If your flight lands in the afternoon, or after midday in winter, leave the boat for another day. A summer morning arrival with a Sunset Trip around 20:00 is the one arrival day plan with real room in it.</p><h2>Why does the departure day work better?</h2><p>Because the risk is on the other side. If the sea is not safe that morning, the skipper cancels, you take the full refund, and you still catch your plane. And if your flight is delayed, nothing about the boat changes.</p><p>The only question is time. Airlines usually ask you to be at the airport about two hours before an international flight. Add 20 to 30 minutes for the taxi and about an hour to shower, change and collect your bags.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Your flight leaves</th><th>Best trip</th><th>Back at the marina</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Before about 16:00</td><td>None that day. Take the Sunset Trip the evening before.</td><td>2h or 2h30 after leaving</td></tr><tr><td>From about 16:00</td><td>Day Trip at 10:00, 2h30</td><td>12:30</td></tr><tr><td>From about 17:00</td><td>Day Trip at 10:00, 2h30 or 3h</td><td>12:30 or 13:00</td></tr><tr><td>After about 21:00</td><td>Day Trip at 10:00 or 14:00</td><td>16:30 or 17:00 for the afternoon trip</td></tr><tr><td>Early the next morning</td><td>Sunset Trip the evening before</td><td>2h or 2h30 after leaving</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Chifbay's Day Trip at 10:00 is the most useful slot on a last day: you get the cliffs of Cabo Girão and two swims further west, and the afternoon is still yours when you step off.</p><h2>What about luggage and a shower?</h2><p>Plan both before you book. After the Day Trip you will have swum twice, and salt on the skin is not how you want to spend a flight.</p><ul><li><strong>Bags.</strong> Many hotels in Funchal hold luggage after check out, so ask yours. Planning to come to the marina with luggage? Check with us on WhatsApp before you book, as room for suitcases on board is not something to count on.</li><li><strong>A shower.</strong> Ask your hotel about a late check out, or about using the pool or spa showers after you check out. Some say yes, some charge, some say no.</li><li><strong>Dry clothes.</strong> Keep a full change in a small bag, apart from the wet swim things.</li><li><strong>Sun.</strong> Two or three hours on the water before a long flight is a lot of sun. Wear a hat and put sun cream on again after swimming.</li></ul><p>The <a href="/practical">practical page with the meeting point and what to bring</a> has the rest.</p><h2>When is it better to skip the boat on travel days?</h2><p>It depends on the group. Leave the boat out of your first and last days if you travel with a baby or toddler, if someone in the group is a nervous flyer who needs a calm day, or if the forecast for your last morning shows a big swell. On a stay of four days or more, the middle of the week is the easy choice, and you can move the trip if the weather turns. If you are torn between slots, read <a href="/posts/morning-or-afternoon-boat-trip-madeira">morning or afternoon boat trip</a>, then book the <a href="/hidden-coves-half-day">Day Trip west of Funchal</a> or the <a href="/sunset-cruise">evening trip at sunset</a>.</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>How long does it take from Madeira airport to Funchal?</h3><p>Usually 20 to 30 minutes by taxi for roughly 16 to 18 km, longer at busy times. The airport bus is slower.</p><h3>Where do diverted Madeira flights go?</h3><p>Usually to Porto Santo, the Canary Islands or mainland Portugal, until the wind drops or the flight is rescheduled.</p><h3>Can I bring my suitcase on the boat?</h3><p>Ask us on WhatsApp before booking. Many hotels in Funchal hold luggage after check out, which is often the simpler option.</p><h3>What is the earliest flight that works after the morning Day Trip?</h3><p>From about 16:00 with the 2h30 trip, back at 12:30. From about 17:00, the 3h trip back at 13:00 fits too.</p>

      <blockquote>Land, sleep, then sail. Sail, shower, then fly.</blockquote>
    </article>
